{"id": "EUVD-2026-55604", "enisaUuid": "74e059f3-0a93-366f-8fe6-34a527b9bb38", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/irdma: Prevent user-triggered null deref on QP create\n\nPreviously, the user QP creation path would only attempt to\npopulate iwqp->iwpbl if the user-provided req.user_wqe_bufs\nfield was non-zero. The problem is that iwqp->iwpbl is\nunconditionally dereferenced later on in irdma_setup_virt_qp.\n\nWhile there was a check for iwqp->iwpbl != NULL, this check\nwould only occur if req.user_wqe_bufs was non-zero. The end\nresult is that a user could send a zero user_wqe_bufs value\nand trigger a null ptr deref.\n\nFix this by unconditionally calling irdma_get_pbl and bailing\nif it fails, similar to the CQ and SRQ paths.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d52ff592abfcd56234f266aa245c489f70b1c554", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad68e0b759f9569f0dfea84f035c91eadb979802", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec675b4cdfd378d8c9dd8c93126c024f2469bd79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/728211c815f6eef28dd3df2a5b6297483185aa20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9b0889071569d43623c260074e159cd8f26adb1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pfxp-3rpf-8hx8", "CVE-2026-68418"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "135e65bb-a901-319d-8b9b-8f2e78fdc67b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b48c24c2d710cf34810c555dcef883a3d35a9c08 <ad68e0b759f9569f0dfea84f035c91eadb979802"}, {"id": "15e53fc6-d9fe-3e51-95d2-6e23851917a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b48c24c2d710cf34810c555dcef883a3d35a9c08 <b9b0889071569d43623c260074e159cd8f26adb1"}, {"id": "2b917c79-8042-345e-96e4-5263b760ebc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2f5c8f20-61f8-3d14-b533-ebbcd12a8efa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b48c24c2d710cf34810c555dcef883a3d35a9c08 <ec675b4cdfd378d8c9dd8c93126c024f2469bd79"}, {"id": "9ca7c54b-c3da-3e1f-a4bc-cfa142d3ed97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a8d249d5-501a-3ecd-81a8-99f13022a1af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "c3c465e7-378d-33a9-9cfa-a411c68a8220", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b48c24c2d710cf34810c555dcef883a3d35a9c08 <728211c815f6eef28dd3df2a5b6297483185aa20"}, {"id": "d7bbab78-3d39-3366-b601-0566b764c6cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "dbd690a8-6ab9-3d07-81eb-119d914d3ac7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b48c24c2d710cf34810c555dcef883a3d35a9c08 <d52ff592abfcd56234f266aa245c489f70b1c554"}, {"id": "f0b2518f-50ba-31e8-81ba-7a292db4237b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "f1dfc45c-8699-37a5-9265-49e777f6b661", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "feb41b79-1304-38b8-ac82-e9a18f74d548", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d10ef91d-df0d-3bed-a4e3-57d6b10ab9dc", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}